## Renaming the C symbol with `extern "C"("name")`. The kaikai
## side calls the function `c_abs`; the linker resolves against
## libc's `abs`. Since `abs` is already declared by the system
## headers (int abs(int)), the binding uses the exact C type:
## I32, not Int.

extern "C"("abs") fn c_abs(n: I32) : I32 / Ffi

fn main() : Unit / Console + Ffi {
  print("|-7| = #{c_abs(0 - 7)}")
}
